ht)}\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{a}{2 \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\cot\\beta\\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression step by step:\n\n\\[\nr^2 = \\left(\\frac{a}{2 \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)}\\right)^2 = \\frac{a^2}{4 \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nr^2 h = \\frac{a^2}{4 \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\times \\frac{a}{2 \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\cot\\beta = \\frac{a^3}{8 \\sin^3\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\cot\\beta\n\\]\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\times \\frac{a^3}{8 \\sin^3\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\cot\\beta = \\frac{\\pi a^3}{24 \\sin^3\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} \\cot\\beta\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the cone is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\pi a^3 \\cot \\beta}{24 \\sin^3 \\dfrac{\\alpha}{2}}}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\nLet's find the volume of the cone given the conditions in the problem:\n\n1. Let $SAK$ be the cone, \\( SO \\) be its height, and \\( BK \\) be a chord with \\( BK=a \\) and \\( \\angle BnK = \\alpha \\) radians. The height \\( SO \\) makes angle \\( \\beta \\) with the conic surface. \n\n2. Let \\( R \\) be the radius of the cone's base. Then, within the triangle \\( OBK \\):\n\n    - Since \\( \\angle BOK = \\alpha \\), we use the Law of Cosines:\n      \\[\n      a^{2} = 2R^{2} - 2R^{2}\\cos(\\alpha).\n      \\]\n\n3. Using the trigonometric identity \\( \\cos(\\alpha) = 1 - 2 \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right) \\):\n    \\[\n    a^2 = 2R^2 \\left[1 - \\left(1 - 2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)\\right)\\right],\n    \\]\n    which simplifies to:\n    \\[\n    a^2 = 2R^2 \\cdot 2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right),\n    \\]\n    hence,\n    \\[\n    a = 2R \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right),\n    \\]\n    and solving for \\( R \\):\n    \\[\n    R = \\frac{a}{2 \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)}.\n    \\]\n\n4. Using triangle \\( SOK \\), the height \\( SO \\) is given by:\n    \\[\n    SO = OK \\cot(\\beta)