ker works twice as fast \\((2b)\\), the work equation is:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{2}a + 2b + c + d\\right) \\times 4 = 1.\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2}a + 2b + c + d = \\frac{1}{4}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **System of Equations:**\n   Now, we have three equations:\n   \\[\n   a + b + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   2a + \\frac{1}{2}b + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{1}{2}a + 2b + c + d = \\frac{1}{4}.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve the Equations:**\n   Subtract the first equation from the second:\n   \\[\n   (2a + \\frac{1}{2}b + c + d) - (a + b + c + d) = 0,\\\\\n   2a + \\frac{1}{2}b - a - b = 0,\\\\\n   a - \\frac{1}{2}b = 0,\\\\\n   a = \\frac{1}{2}b.\n   \\]\n   Subtract the first equation from the third:\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{1}{2}a + 2b + c + d\\right) - \\left(a + b + c + d\\right) = \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{1}{2}a + 2b - a - b = \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   -\\frac{1}{2}a + b = \\frac{1}{12},\\\\\n   -\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\frac{1}{2}b\\right) + b = \\frac{1}{12},\\\\\n   -\\frac{1}{4}b + b = \\frac{1}{12},\\\\\n   \\frac{3}{4}b = \\frac{1}{12},\\\\\n   b = \\frac{1}{12} \\div \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} \\times \\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{1}{9}.\n   \\]\n   Now, \\(a = \\frac{1}{2}b = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{1}{18}\\).\n\n7. **Calculate Work Rate c + d:**\n   We know that:\n   \\[\n   a + b + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{1}{18} + \\frac{1}{9} + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{1}{18} + \\frac{2}{18} + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{3}{18} + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   \\frac{1}{6} + c + d = \\frac{1}{6},\\\\\n   c + d = 0.\n   \\]\n   Thus, the productivity of the third and fourth workers is zero, meaning they did no work.\n\n8. **Conclusion:**\n   The trench will be dug in the same time irrespective by reducing to the first three workers in the given scenarios. Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{6\\text{ hours}}.\n   \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "