ght]\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the determinant**:\n   \\[\n   [\\overrightarrow{IG}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( [\\overrightarrow{IA}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] + [\\overrightarrow{IB}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] + [\\overrightarrow{IC}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] \\right)\n   \\]\n   Since \\([\\overrightarrow{IC}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = 0\\),\n   \\[\n   [\\overrightarrow{IG}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = \\frac{1}{3} \\left( [\\overrightarrow{IA}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] + [\\overrightarrow{IB}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] \\right)\n   \\]\n\n7. **Relate the products to lengths and the inradius**:\n   Using the standard properties of determinants and vectors in triangles, we have:\n   \\[\n   [\\overrightarrow{IA}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = \\text{length }(IA) \\cdot \\text{length }(IC) \\cdot \\text{sin}\\theta = a \\cdot r\n   \\]\n   and\n   \\[\n   [\\overrightarrow{IB}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = \\text{length }(IB) \\cdot \\text{length }(IC) \\cdot \\text{sin}\\phi = - b \\cdot r\n   \\]\n   (negative sign because of the opposite direction).\n\n8. **Combine the results**:\n   \\[\n   [\\overrightarrow{IG}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] = \\frac{1}{3} (ar - br) = \\frac{1}{3} (a - b) r\n   \\]\n\n9. **Calculate the area**:\n   \\[\n   |GIC| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| [\\overrightarrow{IG}, \\overrightarrow{IC}] \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\frac{1}{3} (a - b) r \\right| = \\frac{1}{6} \\left| a - b \\right| r\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{|a - b| r}{6}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "From a point \\( O \\) on a plane, there are 4 rays extending in a clockwise order: \\( OA, OB, OC \\), and \\( OD \\). It is known that the sum of angles \\( \\angle AOB \\) and \\( \\angle COD \\) is \\( 180^\\circ \\). Prove that the bisectors of angles \\( \\angle AOC \\) and \\( \\angle BOD \\) are perpendicular.", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let's try to tackle this geometry problem. So, we have four r